# ── DOCS  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project documentation is version-controlled (AGENTS.md §53/54 requires maintaining
# docs/application-automation/). The blanket *.md rule swallowed the entire docs/ tree once —
# 54 documents were never committed — and was never actually fixed: only AGENTS.md was
# excepted, so every *new* .md was still dropped silently, with no error and no diff to notice.
#
# Policy: `*.md` guards against stray scratch notes at the repo root; `docs/` is tracked in
# full; the repo-mandated root documents are named explicitly. Note that ignore rules do not
# apply to already-tracked files, which is exactly why the old rule looked harmless.
#
# Measured 2026-09-27 — this surfaces precisely the 3 previously-invisible docs/ files.
# `.claude/**` and `brag-output/**` stay ignored via their own directory rules. See
# server_bugs.md SB-15.
*.md
!AGENTS.md
!server_bugs.md
!refactor_audit.md
!/docs/**
# The `!/docs/**` negation above re-includes *everything* under docs/, including the OS metadata
# the earlier `.DS_Store` rule would otherwise have caught (verified: `git check-ignore docs/.DS_Store`
# pointed at the negation). Later rules win, so re-assert it here rather than relying on the top rule.
**/.DS_Store

